 "narrative": "Declared 2019 winter soft wheat -> 2020 silo corn -> 2022 winter soft wheat -> 2023 winter rape -> 2024 clover grass / silo corn -> 2025 winter soft wheat. Untracked years inferred from embeddings (LOYO group acc ~0.9): 2021 ~sugar beet. 4 crops in 6 declared years, cereal share 50%, longest same-crop run 1y; 0 declared-vs-phenology disagreement(s). After summer harvest the field was green over winter in 2/3 seasons (2019 cover/catch, 2022 autumn-sown next crop). Season greenness vs same-crop peers within 5 km: mean percentile 0.60 over 5 years (1 bottom-quartile, 2 top-quartile); weak persistence (A3), treat as season outcomes. Within-field: a stable pattern (year-to-year rho 0.57, 5 seasons); 21% of the field is low-vigour in >=60% of seasons (chance 5.8%), concentrated N. Vigour rises toward lower ground (rho -0.81 vs rotated-DEM null 0.65, relief 6.1 m). Screen flags (unverified, ~27% in-season precision outside vegetables): 2023 delayed_resown."
